# Version & updates popup on every push

When you commit and push user-facing changes to this repo (especially `main`):

1. Bump `utils/app_version.py` (`VERSION_MINOR` or `VERSION_PATCH`, `ESTIMATED_UPDATE_COUNT`, `RELEASE_LABEL` if the day changed).
2. Update the System Updates popup in both:
   - `frontend/src/components/updates/PortalUpdatesHost.tsx` (SPA) — bump `SESSION_KEY`, refresh `LATEST_UPDATES`, fallbacks for `display` / estimate
   - `templates/shared/home.html` — intro + top update section bullets; bump the `sessionStorage` key so the modal shows again
3. If SPA UI changed, rebuild (`cd frontend && npm run build`) and commit `static/spa/` with the release.
4. Include the version bump in the same push (or immediately after) so production shows the new badge and notes.

Do not skip this for “small” fixes that users will notice (bugs, security, roster, Classroom, grading, auth).
